---
title: Split Yellow Moong Dal Khichdi
servings: 4
time: 30 minutes
author: Vedant
---

Wash and soak @split yellow moong dal{1%cup} and @rice{1%cup} for ~{10%minutes}. Drain and keep aside.

In an #Instapot{}, heat @ghee{1/4%cup} and add @cumin seeds (jeera){1/2%tsp}, @hing{1%pinch}, @cloves{4%pcs}, @cinnamon sticks{2%pcs}, and @bay leaves{2%pcs}. Stir until the seeds crackle.

Add @cauliflower florets{1%cup}, @chinese eggplant{1%pc} (diced), @potatoes{1%pc} (peeled and diced), @french beans{3/4%cup}, @onions{1/2%pc} (diced), and @green peas{1/2%cup}. 

Season with @turmeric powder (haldi){1/2%tsp}, @chilli powder{1%tsp}, and @salt{} to taste. Stir for a few minutes.

Add the drained rice and dal and stir until the @ghee coats the grains evenly.

Add @water{4%cups} and stir well. 

#Pressure cook{} for ~{15%minutes}. 

Allow the steam to escape before opening the lid. Mix well and serve hot with @plain yogurt{} and @papad{}.